c{∂}{∂x}(-\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}})=-\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}} \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}})=-\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we denote $F=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩,$ then\n\n$$\nP={z}^{2}={x}^{2}+{y}^{2},\\,Q=0,\\,R=-x.\n$$\n\n \n\nAs a result, since the positive orientation is upward, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{{S}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\cdot (-\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}})-(0)\\cdot (-\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}})+(-x))\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(x\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}-x)\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Consider the lower cylinder ${S}_{2}.$ \n\nWe compute the partial derivatives of $z=h(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂h}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{2}-2)=0 \\\\ \\frac{∂h}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}-2)=2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we denote $F=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩,$ then\n\n$$\nP={z}^{2}={({y}^{2}-2)}^{2},\\,Q=0,\\,R=-x.\n$$\n\n \n\nAs a result, since the positive orientation is downward, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{{S}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & =-{∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂h}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂h}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-{∬}_{D}(-{({y}^{2}-2)}^{2}\\cdot (0)+0\\cdot (2y)+(-x))\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-{∬}_{D}(-x)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}x\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the flux across the entire surface is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{{S}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S+{∬}_{{S}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(x\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}-x)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{D}x\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}x\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405154 1068 #edb/ref 17592186405155 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405154 1069 "q-32876" 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405154 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405154 1071 "Which of the following