db/ref 17592186045499 13194139533501 17592186405019 false] [17592186405202 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405202 1084 #uuid "2016a2e2-9e4e-5a38-9fa3-a7d1bc597b90" 13194139533501 17592186405019 false] [17592186405202 1084 #uuid "2016a2e2-9e4e-5a38-9fa3-a7d1bc597b90" 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405203 1068 #edb/ref 17592186405204 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405203 1069 "q-97990" 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405203 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405203 1071 "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ and the quadratic curve ${x}^{T}\\,Ax=7.$ Given that $A$ has eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=2$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-3,$ find the principal axes of the curve." 13194139533501 17592186405019 false] [17592186405203 1071 "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ and the quadratic curve ${x}^{T}\\,Ax=7.$ Given that $A$ has eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=2$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-3,$ find the principal axes of the curve." 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405203 1071 "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ and the quadratic curve ${x}^{T}\\,Ax=7.$ Given that $A$ has eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=2$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-3,$ find unit vectors along the principal axes of the curve corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{1}$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}$, respectively." 13194139533501 17592186405019 true] [17592186405203 1072 #uuid "5fb95d9e-0ced-5515-baa2-9595c0717556" 13194139533500 17592186045585 true] [17592186405203 1074 "Notice that $A$ is symmetric. \nThe principal axes of the curve \n\n$$\n{x}^{T}\\,Ax=7\n$$\n\nare the vectors that give an orthonormal eigenvector basis for $A.$ Let's now find these eigenvectors.\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-2I & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \